I have noticed that a decent pudding farming FAQ/spoiler doesnt seem
to exist.
I noticed this because I just found a great way of farming and I'm
sure im not the first one to have done this.
How does everyone else here do their farming?

heres my method,feel free to improve it or spot the problems with
it...

I found a level with an altar and a sink (you can reverse-genocide
instead of a sink). If the altar isnt co-aligned,kill the priest and
convert it.
First I dig out about half the level (around the altar) using wands
and a pick-axe and I light as much as possible with wand of light.
I then built a fortress around the altar with 1 empty space behind the
altar, leave an entrance for 1 pudding at a time. This way you stand
behind the altar and poke the puddings on the altar and you cant get
swarmed by other random monsters.
Now before you start farming make sure you have a decent AC, damage
proof armour and a ring of slow digestion (this will take a long
time). Some K-rations wouldnt hurt either.Oh and dont forget a crappy
disposable weapon, I use a dagger!

Kick the sink until a black pudding comes along.now,remove gauntlets
of power(or rings of increase damage),wield a crappy dagger (what IS
the most ineffective weapon anyway?) and poke the pudding. It should
split. Now,your puddings are weak so leave them alone for a while,
this is the trickiest part, you must never kill your whole crop!
(unless you're finished farming)
After about 20 or so turns poke both of them,you should have four
now.remember which ones have just been spawned or poked and leave them
alone, theyre weak.
Repeat until you have about 20-30 puddings (dont let yourself get
surrounded while youre doing this).
Once you have about 20-30, retreat into your fortress and let them
enter.
Stand behind the altar and poke the pudding that is on the altar with
your crappy knife. It will probably split and then die, sometimes they
die without splitting, sometimes they split once and die, sometimes
they split 2-3 times (more?).let the next pudding step forward and
repeat. When you get a chance step forward onto the altar ,sacrifice
all the puddings there, pick up all the items (B/U/C ID them if you
want).
Dont let too many puddings die in a row on the altar because if one
rots youre screwed! (the most I've tried is 14).
This seems to work pretty well, I pray to my god every 30 corpses or
so and get all gifts from prayers and sacrifices.The puddings
themselves drop off all kinds of goodies.

Does anyone know what the odds are of a pudding bringing you an item?
The odds of a magical tool or armour? Scrolls? Potions?
How much does a black puddding corpse 'lower' your prayer timeout?
What is the ideal amount of corpses to wait between prayers?

Suggestions?

